    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fe624e6d-9fc8-53a0-b54d-a6cda07c5265",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+12y &=36 \\\\ 5x+11y &=41.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 41\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 41\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 41\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
